  "title": "RFC 2198: Process later codecs after an exception",
  "description": "If we get an nonfatal error when processing a secondary codec,\nreport it and continue on to the next codec. That particular codec\ngot an error, but the we know the length and payload type from\nearlier in the header, so it shouldn't stop us from dissecting\nthe primary codec.\n\nDo abort on Errors that do mean that there's no point in continuing.",
